  - IVTFF
  - digital humanities
  - historical linguistics
abstract: >
  The Voynich Transliteration Tool (TVTT) is a workbench for building, testing
  and stress-testing substitution mappings for the Voynich Manuscript. It parses
  the published IVTFF transliterations in full, preserving folio, paragraph and
  locus information, so that analyses can be restricted to named manuscript
  sections, Currier languages, individual scribes, labels or first lines.

  Beyond applying a mapping, TVTT measures the result: conditional entropy,
  word-length distribution, vocabulary growth, Zipf and Heaps behaviour,
  positional and slot-grammar structure, affixes, repetition and line-position
  effects. Its distinguishing feature is a suite of baselines intended to
  prevent false positives, including random-mapping control distributions,
  shuffled-text baselines, a synthetic self-citation generator used as a null
  hypothesis, real-language controls, held-out validation and an overfitting
  warning. It also provides dictionary matching with significance testing, and
  hill-climbing, simulated-annealing and genetic solvers.

  Every run writes a manifest recording the tool version, configuration hash,
  input checksums and random seed, so that results are reproducible and citable.
